fund-java/05-interfaces-and-inheritance/.explanation:
The limit check uses `cents` while the account is debited `cents + fee`. A savings withdrawal of the whole balance therefore passes the check and leaves the balance negative by the fee: "savings never goes negative" withdraws 1000 from 1000 and expects an IllegalStateException that never comes. The checking tests pass, because a checking fee is 0 and the two amounts are equal there. Check the same total you then subtract:

```java
long total = cents + fee(cents);
if (balance - total < -overdraftLimit()) throw new IllegalStateException("insufficient funds");
balance -= total;
```

Moving the check after the subtraction, instead of before it, is a different bug: it fails "savings never goes negative" and "checking refuses one cent past the limit (boundary)", because a refused withdrawal has already changed the balance.
